    "### 1. Abelian Groups\n",
    "- **Addition $(\\mathbb{Z}, +)$**:\n",
    "  - Closure: $a+b$ is an integer for all $a, b \\in \\mathbb{Z}$.\n",
    "  - Associativity: $(a+b)+c = a+(b+c)$ holds.\n",
    "  - Identity: $0 \\in \\mathbb{Z}$ is the identity since $a+0 = a$.\n",
    "  - Inverse: For any $a \\in \\mathbb{Z}$, $-a \\in \\mathbb{Z}$ is the inverse since $a+(-a) = 0$.\n",
    "  - Commutativity: $a+b = b+a$ holds.\n",
    "  Hence, it is an abelian group.\n",
    "- **Multiplication $(\\mathbb{Z}, \\times)$**:\n",
    "  - The identity is 1. However, elements like 2 have no multiplicative inverse in $\\mathbb{Z}$ (since $1/2 \\notin \\mathbb{Z}$). Thus, it is not a group."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Conceptual verification."
   ]
  },
  {
