    "### 4. Equivariance vs Invariance\n",
    "A function $f: X \\to Y$ is invariant under group action $G$ if $f(g \\cdot x) = f(x)$ for all $g \\in G$ and $x \\in X$.\n",
    "Let $w = h \\circ f$. Then:\n",
    "$$w(g \\cdot x) = h(f(g \\cdot x))$$\n",
    "Since $f(g \\cdot x) = f(x)$:\n",
    "$$h(f(g \\cdot x)) = h(f(x)) = w(x)$$\n",
    "Hence, $h \\circ f$ is also invariant under $G$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Proof verified."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5. Vector Space Axioms\n",
    "Let $V = \\{f : \\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}\\}$. \n",
    "- Addition: $(f+g)(x) = f(x) + g(x)$ is a function from $\\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$.\n",
    "- Scalar multiplication: $(cf)(x) = c \\cdot f(x)$ is a function from $\\mathbb{R} \\to \\mathbb{R}$.\n",
    "All vector space axioms (commutativity, associativity, zero function, additive inverse, distributivity) are inherited directly from the field of real numbers $\\mathbb{R}$. For instance, the zero vector is the function $z(x) = 0$ for all $x$."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Explanation verified."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6. Category Axioms\n",
    "Let $\\mathcal{C}$ be the category of matrices:\n",
    "- Objects: $\\mathbb{N}$.\n",
    "- Morphisms: For $n, m \\in \\mathbb{N}$, a morphism $f: n \\to m$ is a real matrix $M \\in \\mathbb{R}^{m \\times n}$.\n",
    "- Identity: The identity morphism for object $n$ is the $n \\times n$ identity matrix $I_n$.\n",
    "- Composition: Given $f: n \\to m$ (matrix $B$) and $g: m \\to p$ (matrix $A$), their composition $g \\circ f$ is the matrix multiplication $A \\cdot B$, which is a $p \\times n$ matrix, thus a morphism $n \\to p$.\n",
    "- Associativity: Matrix multiplication is associative: $C(BA) = (CB)A$. Identity law: $A I = I A = A$ holds."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Explanation verified."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 7. Functors in Functional Programming"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class FunctorList:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, data):\n",
    "        self.data = list(data)\n",
    "\n",
    "    def map(self, func):\n",
    "        return FunctorList([func(x) for x in self.data])\n",
    "\n",
    "    def __repr__(self):\n",
    "        return f\"List({self.data})\"\n",
    "\n",
    "identity = lambda x: x\n",
    "lst = FunctorList([1, 2, 3])\n",
    "mapped_lst = lst.map(identity)\n",
    "print(\"Original:\", lst)\n",
    "print(\"Mapped:  \", mapped_lst)\n",
    "print(\"Identity law holds?\", lst.data == mapped_lst.data)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 8. Group Homomorphism\n",
    "For $x, y \\in \\mathbb{R}^+$:\n",
    "$$\\log(x \\times y) = \\log(x) + \\log(y)$$\n",
    "Since the mapping preserves the binary operation (mapping multiplication in the domain to addition in the codomain), it is a group homomorphism."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
