    "### 9. Permutation Invariance in GNNs\n",
    "For a permutation matrix $P$, we have $P^T P = I$. The degree matrix of $P A P^T$ is $P D PAP^T$ since degree is invariant under node renaming.\n",
    "$$f(P A P^T, P X) = (P D P^T)^{-1/2} (P A P^T) (P D P^T)^{-1/2} (P X) W$$\n",
    "$$= P D^{-1/2} P^T P A P^T P D^{-1/2} P^T P X W$$\n",
    "$$= P D^{-1/2} A D^{-1/2} X W = P f(A, X)$$\n",
    "Hence, GCN propagation is permutation equivariant."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Proof verified."
   ]
