    "### 10. Group Equivariant CNNs (G-CNNs)\n",
    "Group Equivariant CNNs extend translation equivariance by ensuring that the network layers commute with other transformations (such as rotations, reflections, or scale shifts). This is achieved by defining the convolution operation over a symmetry group $G$ rather than just the translation group $\\mathbb{R}^2$."
   ]
  },
  {
