  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 13. The Monad Laws"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "class Maybe:\n",
    "    def __init__(self, value):\n",
    "        self.value = value\n",
    "    def bind(self, func):\n",
    "        if self.value is None: return Maybe(None)\n",
    "        return func(self.value)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Left Identity: return x >>= f  ==  f x\n",
    "f = lambda x: Maybe(x + 1)\n",
    "x = 5\n",
    "lhs = Maybe(x).bind(f).value\n",
    "rhs = f(x).value\n",
    "print(\"Left identity holds:\", lhs == rhs)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Right Identity: m >>= return  ==  m\n",
    "m = Maybe(10)\n",
    "lhs = m.bind(lambda y: Maybe(y)).value\n",
    "rhs = m.value\n",
    "print(\"Right identity holds:\", lhs == rhs)\n",
    "\n",
    "# 3. Associativity: (m >>= f) >>= g  ==  m >>= (\\lambda x -> f x >>= g)\n",
    "g = lambda x: Maybe(x * 2)\n",
    "lhs = m.bind(f).bind(g).value\n",
    "rhs = m.bind(lambda y: f(y).bind(g)).value\n",
    "print(\"Associativity holds:\", lhs == rhs)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 14. Universal Property of Tensor Product\n",
    "The universal property states that for any bilinear map $f: V \\times W \\to U$, there exists a unique linear map $\\tilde{f}: V \\otimes W \\to U$ such that $f(v, w) = \\tilde{f}(v \\otimes w)$. This allows us to convert multi-linear operations (e.g. bilinear attention queries) into standard matrix multiplications (linear maps) on the tensor product space."
   ]
  },
