    "### 15. Compositional Generalization in NLP\n",
    "DisCoCat (Distributional Compositional Categorical) models combine grammar rules (which form a monoidal category) with word meanings (vectors). By defining functors from the category of grammar to the category of vector spaces, the meaning of a sentence is computed compositionally as a tensor contraction of word vectors according to the grammatical structure of the sentence."
